<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bao Si</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bao Si was a consort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-you-of-zhou">King You of Zhou</a> in the 8th century BCE. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/records-of-the-grand-historian">Shiji</a>, the king deposed Queen Shen and the crown prince in favour of her and her son, and lit the warning beacons to make her laugh until the lords no longer answered them. The Marquis of Shen then allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanrong">Quanrong</a> to sack the capital in 771 BCE, ending the Western Zhou.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bao-si.jpg" alt="Bao Si" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wang Hui 王翙 (1736-1795) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bao_Si_-_Bai_Mei_Xin_Yong.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
